# Intent: Overlay readability pass, part 1, the engine (owner brief 2026-11-17: at arm's length the overlays were too small and thin). Every element is rebuilt from the core's size functions: zzz are filled glyphs with a darker outline in three sizes (24, 36 and 48 px, rising in the columns beside the eyes and fading at the top), rain is 3 px wide and 14 to 24 px long, snow flakes are 5 to 10 px, clouds are 96 to 156 px wide in a back and a front layer (a quarter of the screen at heavy, drifting two pixels at a time), the sun is 52 px with 16 turning rays, fireworks open to 60 to 100 px with a flash, a spark head and a six-dot trail, hearts are 24, 32 and 40 px with an outline and a shine, confetti pieces are 8 to 14 px, leaves are 14 px with a vein, wind is a curled streak up to 7 px thick with a second streak under it, fog is four soft bands, stars and sparkles are four-point stars of 8 to 16 px. Two new parts (a crescent moon and sparkles) and ten named combinations (stormy, rainy, snowy, sunny, windy, night, party, celebrate, love, sleeping) run on three layers (weather, event, front) that draw front to back; one overlay of its own replaces what runs in its layer and ends a combination. Every overlay is behind the face: a pixel is painted only on a background pixel, the first paint of a pixel wins (a front cloud, a fill before its outline), the canvas can keep the banner row (y 0 to 27) and the subtitle strip (y 184 to 239) free (mc_t.ztop and zbot) and can protect ellipses around the eyes and the mouth (a pupil and an open mouth are dark but not background), and the thunder flash lights the sky and the clouds but not the face. Falling things move every second tick, twice as far (15 pictures a second halve the flushed pixels), the draw order of particles never changes without a repaint (ordered removal), and the dirty rectangles cover every changed pixel (a host test compares a partial flush with a full redraw for every overlay and combination). The palette and the anchors live in one table the settings page preview draws from (host/tests/firmware/overlay_dump.c prints it as overlay_table.json). Costs: three layers are 2.76 KB of state in PSRAM (was 1.35 KB), internal RAM adds nothing; modeled flush cost per overlay and combination is in docs/design/overlays-2026-11-17.md and the governor halves the particles of every one of them.
# Placement: unit (the overlays run on the robot with no host)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/maipai_overlay_core.h (ours, patch TA03)
# Check after a flash: self.overlay.set for each of the 26 names, then scripts/fw-serial.py snap on every style: nothing drawn over an eye, the mouth, the banner row or the subtitle strip; the host renderer sheets (scripts/fw-face-render/overlays_render.sh) show the same pictures; self.overlay.status reports the governor shedding under load.

